{"type":"message","id":"678b5c4a","parentId":"d6290859","timestamp":"2026-06-25T05:39:41.393Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I should provide a summary to the group but actually, according to the FEED_DRAIN entry in SOUL.md, I should end the turn silently:\n\n\"- **Chain the next story, then END the turn** — clear this cron's lease and re-run the dispatcher. If more jobs are queued it sets the lease and fires a fresh isolated FEED_DRAIN cron (new context) for the next one; if the queue is empty it prints `DISPATCH_IDLE` and nothing fires:\n\nThen end the turn silently. Tap = approval; each article auto-publishes to a WordPress DRAFT + posts the news card. Do **not** wait for user input.\"\n\nSo I should end with NO_REPLY. Let me check if there are any messages I need to send. According to SOUL.md for FEED_DRAIN runs (which have STEP25_GATE=OFF), the stories are auto-published to draft + card with no per-story gate. The dispatch is already done.\n\nActually wait - I should send a group message about the success. Let me check the Step 2.6 flow - it says to send to the project's group:\n\n\"Reply to the project's group `$GROUP_CHAT_ID` (via the `message` tool) (success):\n```\nStory $PICK_INDEX published to WordPress draft (published $PUBLISHED/$TARGET).\n\nDraft: [actual WordPress URL]\nStatus: Draft - use Telegram card to Publish when ready.\n```\"\n\nWait, let me re-read - that's for STEP25_GATE=ON. For FEED_DRAIN where STEP25_GATE=OFF, we skip Step 2.5 and go to Step 2.6. But there's no explicit mention of sending a group message in FEED_DRAIN flow...\n\nActually looking at the card - build_and_send_card.py already sent a card to the group, which serves as the notification.\n\nLet me see - the FEED_DRAIN entry in SOUL.md says:\n\"Chain the next story, then END the turn — clear this cron's lease and re-run the dispatcher...Then end the turn silently.\"\n\n\nSince build_and_send_card.py already delivered the notification 